#: src/self-hosted.md:76
msgid "Caveats"
msgstr ""

#: src/self-hosted.md:78
msgid ""
"In this section, we explain existing problems of using self-hosted "
"development and a possible workaround for it."
msgstr ""

#: src/self-hosted.md:80
msgid "No recovery point"
msgstr ""

#: src/self-hosted.md:82
msgid ""
"Redox OS currently has no mechanism for recovering itself if a build broke "
"the system. Before that happens, it's a good idea to have a backup or "
"prepare a clean image from the daily build."
msgstr ""

#: src/self-hosted.md:84
msgid ""
"Having a secondary Linux OS in the same system can ease recovering the "
"system from an unbootable position. See [RedoxFS: Working with Linux "
"Partition](./redoxfs.md#working-with-linux-partition) for more details."
msgstr ""

#: src/self-hosted.md:86
msgid "No GCC \"Cross compiler\" mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/self-hosted.md:88
msgid ""
"GCC that's built for Linux is configured as \"Cross compiler\" mode, whereas "
"GCC that's built for Redox is configured as \"Hosted compiler\". The "
"difference between these two modes affects which `relibc` variant is used "
"during compilation, and in this case the GCC uses the `relibc` from the "
"system installed at `/usr` to do the compilation, instead of the expected "
"place in the `prefix` directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/self-hosted.md:90
msgid ""
"There is no way to change the mode to \"Cross compiler\" without rebuilding, "
"so the easiest way to fix it is by using Clang as the default compiler. Add "
"this config to `.config` to change that:"
msgstr ""

